@startuml

title The provision request: the fields the caller supplies

class "provision tenant request\n(iam.v1.ops.provision_tenant)" as provision_request <<message>> #E1F5FF {
    {field} +starting point : code
    {field} +tenant code : text
    {field} +tenant name : text
    {field} +tenant hostname : text
    {field} +tenant description : text
    {field} +administrator username : text
    {field} +administrator email : text
    {field} +administrator password : text
    {field} +parameter values : list
}

class "parameter value" as parameter_value <<message>> #E1F5FF {
    {field} +name : text
    {field} +value : text
}

provision_request *-- "0..*" parameter_value : a list of

note top of provision_request
The one request that provisions a tenant from a starting point.
code starting point // the registered starting point whose operations the run performs
text tenant code // the unique code of the tenant to create
text tenant name // the tenant's display name
text tenant hostname // the hostname a principal resolves its tenant through
text tenant description // an optional description of the tenant record
text administrator username // the first administrator's username, without a hostname part
text administrator email // that administrator's email address
text administrator password // that administrator's initial password
list parameter values // one value for each parameter the starting point's schema declares
end note

note top of parameter_value
One value for one parameter the starting point's schema declares.
text name // the parameter the starting point declares
text value // the value the person supplied for it
end note

@enduml
